{"author":{"id":"1d21e70a32f794e19f8d3626c963a95c52102f79bd1dc44e2b4b611903f1b863"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1781091285,"nonce":"mtNZPsS82xVom7efuR2Yb/6WFNc=","target":"35b245eb9f9e1beba333819b95f48b07ec42bf809fbc30f4b5d4b239e0d73053","message":"okay, just pulled the perfect-commit branch onto nemesis and immediately ran into some issues.\n\nfirstly, ssh-agent was not working. i had to use programs.ssh.startAgent to get the service running, which i assume is running by default on darwin, or at least on auto by the MDM. afterwards, it didnt work cos SSH_AUTH_SOCK was not set, which I had to fix with a reboot. however, the user service we initialised to auto ssh-add on login still fails with could not authenticate with the agent - is this because the env var is not set? need to investigate in the service definition.\n\nverified:\n```console\n❯ git diff HEAD\ndiff --git a/nix/profiles/development.nix b/nix/profiles/development.nix\nindex 6ebf37e..9aeb280 100644\n--- a/nix/profiles/development.nix\n+++ b/nix/profiles/development.nix\n@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ in\n       home-manager.sharedModules = [\n         cfg.modules.homeManager.profile-development\n         (\n-          { pkgs, config, ... }:\n+          { pkgs, ... }:\n           {\n             systemd.user.services.ssh-add = {\n               Unit = {\n@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ in\n               };\n               Service = {\n                 Type = \"oneshot\";\n-                ExecStart = \"${pkgs.openssh}/bin/ssh-add ${config.home.homeDirectory}/.ssh/id_ed25519\";\n+                ExecStart = \"${pkgs.coreutils}/bin/echo $SSH_AUTH_SOCK\";\n                 RemainAfterExit = true;\n               };\n               Install.WantedBy = [ \"default.target\" ];\n❯ systemctl --user status ssh-add\n● ssh-add.service - Add SSH key to agent on login\n     Loaded: loaded (/home/rafiq/.config/systemd/user/ssh-add.service; enabled; preset: ignored)\n     Active: active (exited) since Wed 2026-06-10 19:00:43 +08; 2min 23s ago\n