s\n------\n`git-bug` works great, however I was unable to push to the git remote due to this error: \n\n```sh\nError: ssh: handshake failed: ssh: unable to authenticate, attempted methods [none publickey], no supported methods remain\n```\n\nThe cause of this issue (investigated by Claudius) is that the SSH library that `git-bug` uses only supports authentication with the ssh-agent, not falling back to the SSH key. Thusly, I implemented user services to run `ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519` on login. This didn't work right away on NixOS, as I had to also point SSH_AUTH_SOCK in the service config environment to `%t/ssh-agent`, which is how the NixOS option `programs.ssh.startAgent` persists its agent.\n\nThe TUI is also more ergonomic than the shell commands, so I added `gb` to alias to `git-bug termui`, as well as `gu` and `gy` pulling and pushing for git-bug. Also, I added a custom module to `starship` that will show a 🐛 whenever `git-bug` is out of sync with the remote by checking for \n\nReferences\n----------\n\n- https://simonwillison.net/2022/Oct/29/the-perfect-commit","files":null}]}